We've spent the last two years building something we always wished existed: a single, beautifully crafted app that unifies the three pillars of a reading workflow — RSS feeds, Read Later, and Bookmarks.

## Why another reading app?

The reading tool landscape is fragmented. You have one app for RSS, another for saving articles, a browser for bookmarks, and maybe a separate PDF reader. Each one is fine on its own, but together they create a scattered, stressful experience.

Cardmaniacs brings all of this together in one calm, native Apple app.

## What makes it different

- **Truly native** — Built entirely in Swift for macOS, iOS, and iPadOS. No Electron, no web views.
- **Card-based UI** — Every piece of content is a tactile card on your reading desk.
- **Specialized parsers** — Clean rendering of JS-heavy sites, GitHub READMEs, Wikipedia articles.
- **Power user features** — Vim navigation, keyboard shortcuts, smart folders, and full-text search.

We can't wait for you to try it.
